1
00:00:00,138 --> 00:00:01,238
Three points refuse to

2
00:00:01,238 --> 00:00:02,725
sit on one line.

3
00:00:02,725 --> 00:00:04,162
Which line fits best,

4
00:00:04,162 --> 00:00:04,562
and why does a

5
00:00:04,562 --> 00:00:05,812
right angle decide it?

6
00:00:06,413 --> 00:00:07,512
Through the first point,

7
00:00:07,512 --> 00:00:10,137
the line needs C equals six.

8
00:00:10,137 --> 00:00:11,037
Then point two wants

9
00:00:11,037 --> 00:00:12,800
D equals minus six,

10
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,712
and point three wants minus three.

11
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:16,471
So let it miss.

12
00:00:16,471 --> 00:00:18,958
Least squares tilts and slides the

13
00:00:18,958 --> 00:00:21,496
line until the squared vertical misses

14
00:00:21,496 --> 00:00:23,120
are as small as possible.

15
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,000
It settles on five minus three t,

16
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:28,900
missing by one, minus two and one.

17
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:30,400
Squared, they add to six.

18
00:00:30,987 --> 00:00:32,763
Now stack the three heights

19
00:00:32,763 --> 00:00:34,850
into one arrow b,

20
00:00:34,850 --> 00:00:36,375
in three dimensions.

21
00:00:36,375 --> 00:00:38,038
The heights of every possible

22
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,687
line fill a plane,

23
00:00:39,687 --> 00:00:41,513
spanned by the columns of A.

24
00:00:42,433 --> 00:00:43,608
Straight below b sits

25
00:00:43,608 --> 00:00:47,083
the closest point, p: five, two,

26
00:00:47,083 --> 00:00:47,620
minus one,

27
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,308
the best line's heights.

28
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:50,921
The drop is the error e.

29
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:52,783
So e is perpendicular

30
00:00:52,783 --> 00:00:54,308
to both columns:

31
00:00:54,308 --> 00:00:57,033
one minus two plus one is zero,

32
00:00:57,033 --> 00:00:58,295
and zero minus two

33
00:00:58,295 --> 00:00:59,958
plus two is zero.

34
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:03,230
So A transpose e is zero.

35
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:05,829
Write e as b minus A x hat,

36
00:01:05,829 --> 00:01:07,767
and out come the normal equations:

37
00:01:08,129 --> 00:01:09,405
A transpose A x hat

38
00:01:09,405 --> 00:01:10,929
equals A transpose b.

39
00:01:11,513 --> 00:01:13,200
Here they give C equals five

40
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,400
and D equals minus three:

41
00:01:15,812 --> 00:01:17,300
the same best line,

42
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,563
found by a right angle.
